From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:03:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 26/26] player process info: the video's live bitrate shows

Upstream's label read $INFO[Player.Process(videolivebitrate,$COMMA ,]:
the closing parenthesis missing, so Kodi logged "unmatched parentheses"
each time the panel opened and the video line never showed the bitrate.
The audio line's has it.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 xml/DialogPlayerProcessInfo.xml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xml/DialogPlayerProcessInfo.xml b/xml/DialogPlayerProcessInfo.xml
index fcdcdee..dc518a1 100644
--- a/xml/DialogPlayerProcessInfo.xml
+++ b/xml/DialogPlayerProcessInfo.xml
@@ -155,7 +155,7 @@
 					<width>900</width>
 					<height>40</height>
 					<aligny>bottom</aligny>
-					<label>$INFO[Player.Process(videowidth),[COLOR button_focus]$LOCALIZE[38031]:[/COLOR] ,x]$INFO[Player.Process(videoheight)]$INFO[Player.Process(videoscantype)]$INFO[Player.Process(videodar),$COMMA , AR]$INFO[Player.Process(videofps),$COMMA , FPS]$INFO[Player.Process(videolivebitrate,$COMMA ,]</label>
+					<label>$INFO[Player.Process(videowidth),[COLOR button_focus]$LOCALIZE[38031]:[/COLOR] ,x]$INFO[Player.Process(videoheight)]$INFO[Player.Process(videoscantype)]$INFO[Player.Process(videodar),$COMMA , AR]$INFO[Player.Process(videofps),$COMMA , FPS]$INFO[Player.Process(videolivebitrate),$COMMA ,]</label>
 					<font>font12</font>
 					<shadowcolor>black</shadowcolor>
 				</control>
